  "description": {
   "extraction_status": "extracted",
   "value": "The study validated a modified Empathic Accuracy Task using naturalistic autobiographical emotional videos, continuous ratings of perceived emotional intensity, and a neutral control condition to examine neural correlates of empathy, empathic accuracy, and dynamic emotional tracking.",
   "value_source": "generated"
  },
  "design": {
   "extraction_status": "extracted",
   "value": "In the scanner, 34 healthy participants watched 6 video clips of people talking about an autobiographical event (2 sad, 2 happy and 2 neutral clips) while continuously rating the narrator's emotional intensity. The study used a staged fMRI analysis approach including emotional versus neutral contrasts, empathic accuracy modulation, emotional-intensity correlations, and an exploratory affect-sharing comparison.",
   "value_source": "reported"
  },
